            "text": "CRUX_SURFACE_RE fires 72 times on added Rust lines; the large majority is a sampling-parameter consolidation (temperature/top_k/top_p/seed/repeat_penalty/repeat_last_n) into crates/aprender-common/src/cli_roles.rs (7 clap long= hits there) plus one #[arg(...)]/long= hit each in ~20 CLI entrypoint crates that now reference the shared definitions (apr-cli/src/{commands_enum.rs (10), extended_commands.rs (4), commands/rosetta.rs (2)}, aprender-contracts-cli, aprender-zram-cli, aprender-train-{shell,lora,inspect,distill,bench}, aprender-test-cli, aprender-rag-cli, aprender-qa-cli, aprender-profile, aprender-present-terminal, aprender-present-cli, aprender-orchestrate, aprender-explain, aprender-db, aprender-data, aprender-cgp, aprender-cbtop, apr-cli/src/{surface.rs, serve_commands.rs, commands/gpu_correct_subject.rs}). These flag names are pre-existing CLI surface (same names, same behavior contract); the diff relocates the arg definitions, it does not add new ones. Contract coverage (crux-A-13, crux-A-16, crux-C-30, crux-C-32, crux-F-06, decode-gpu-resident-sampling-v1, batched-beam-search-v1 and 97 more matched on these parameter names) is pre-existing; this review did not re-verify behavioral equivalence of every relocated flag against every one of the 104 matched contracts within its time budget -- that check is asserted from the refactor's shape (identical flag names/defaults visible in the diff), not independently measured flag-by-flag."
          },
