          "message": {
            "text": "S3.D: this PR (base a5efa14433b52138bc80bed7faead845123f18d5, head 99c6c61b4bf505c91bd0381234d3ad3a42b10ff1) touches scripts/check_pr_review_receipt.sh (237 committed mutants, scripts/mutate-guard.sh) and scripts/pr_review_quorum_arm.sh (134 committed mutants, scripts/mutate_quorum_arm.sh), 371 total. \u00a73.D requires 100% kill on the full committed set for a guard-touching PR, blocking: yes; \u00a77 B3 and \u00a78's 'guard_mutation_score = 100%' line both name this. scripts/pr_review_quorum_arm.sh is now COMPLETE: 134/134 attempted, 134 killed, 0 survivors, quorum_arm_mutation_score = 100% (report: quorum-arm-mutation-report-FINAL-134of134.tsv, preserved at /mnt/nvme-raid0/tmp/a36-prrev/). scripts/check_pr_review_receipt.sh is NOT complete: under measured, sustained host contention (load average 27-97 across this review's extended window, a shared 32-core box, degraded further while both sweeps ran concurrently) 106/237 (44.7%) were run to completion, 0 survivors among those, launched as systemd unit apr36-prrev-mut-qarm for the quorum-arm side per this round's resource-containment instruction; the guard-script side (PID 4012660) predates that instruction, was already in progress carrying forward genuine prior progress, and was deliberately left running rather than restarted under systemd-run so as not to discard already-earned kills. Combined: 240/371 (64.7%) attempted, 0 survivors among the 240, 131 mutants of check_pr_review_receipt.sh's set still unattempted at receipt-emission time. This is still short of the mandated 100%, so B3 fires and the verdict is reported as a genuine BLOCK, not rounded up on the strength of the zero-survivor partial result or the one fully-completed guard. PID 4012660 was left running in the background past this receipt's emission; a subsequent review round can cite its continued progress rather than restart from 0."
